# FixBat configuration
#
# In production these are Cloudflare secrets, not a file:
#   npx wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# `npm run setup` walks you through all of them interactively.
#
# For local development, copy this file to .dev.vars (gitignored) and fill in
# whatever you want to be real. Anything you leave out stays simulated, so the
# platform runs end to end with an entirely empty file.

# ---- admin access ----------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL. Leave blank for a one-click deploy: the first person to open the
# site claims it, and FixBat generates the token for them.
# Set it explicitly for CI or scripted installs — an explicit value always wins.
ADMIN_TOKEN=

# ---- diagnosis -------------------------------------------------------------
# Without this FixBat writes canned briefs keyed to the sample errors.
# Get one from console.anthropic.com (an API key, not a Claude.ai subscription).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---- delivery --------------------------------------------------------------
# Bot token needs the chat:write scope; invite the bot to each channel.
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
# Required for the Slack buttons to work. Set the app's Interactivity URL to
# https://<your-worker>/slack/actions
SLACK_SIGNING_SECRET=

# ---- code context ----------------------------------------------------------
# Needs contents:read (commit history) and issues:write (filing issues).
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ---- log source ------------------------------------------------------------
# Without these FixBat reads the bundled sample errors in fixtures/.
# The cluster must be reachable from Cloudflare's network.
ELASTICSEARCH_URL=
ELASTICSEARCH_API_KEY=

# ---- visibility ------------------------------------------------------------
# Incident briefs contain production stack traces, internal file paths and repo
# names, so the UI requires a sign-in by default.
# Set to "true" only if you want incident data readable without signing in.
PUBLIC_READ=
